gressives accept this slim down  bill  it's the bare minimum of what we should  be doing you know certainly what you  know i would prefer is that we abolish  the filibuster and then we pass the john  lewis voting rights act and we pass the  for the people act um so this is um just  the bare minimum of what we really  should be doing i mean after all we're  talking about the disenfranchisement  of millions of voters disproportionately  voters of color  disabled voters and the elderly  progressives are also deeply concerned  about this summer's gop attack on  reproductive rights after rebuffing a  challenge uh the new texas law that  effectively bans abortion six weeks  after conception the supreme court is  now taking up a similar mississippi law  in a case that could put the final nail  in roe versus wade's coffin if there was  ever a strong case for reforming or even  expanding the supreme court isn't it now  why aren't we hearing more about court  reform from the democratic party  well because we have seen the hurt and  harm inflicted by the extremism  of the supreme court um whether you're  talking about housing rights voting  rights or reproductive freedom they have  had uh  by my vintage point contempt uh for the  most vulnerable and are uh working to  erode at uh human and civil rights that  we fought and organized a hard to earn  um and so this is not a new conversation  and in fact it is not even precedent  setting congress has the authority to do  it we've done it seven times uh  congressman mandir jones introduced a  bill of which i'm a co-sponsor um to  expand the courts and so you know what i  would like to see is that we bring to  the floor uh my bill with representative  judy chu i thank her for her leadership  all these many years i chair the  abortion rights and access task force  under the pro-choice caucus this is the  first pro-choice majority congress in  the history of congress that has to mean  something we need to bring the women's  health protection act to the floor for a  vote to codify worldview wade which is  again popular and also necessary for  reproductive freedom and would ban uh  the introduction introduction of other  harmful and draconian state laws like  what in texas  we're almost out of time but i have to  ask a question about your progressive  squad colleague alexandra ocasio-cortez  she set off a social media furore  yesterday after attending the met gala  in a designer dress with the message tax  the rich emblazoned across her back  quite the statement in a gallery full of  money elites what did you make of that  some people are saying she shouldn't  have even gone  well she has a platform and she's using  it uh both to uh steward uh discourse  and debate and to advance policy  and so our cosign tax to rich and again  for those that would argue that for all  of these bold investments that we need  to make in housing care and climate to  meet the moment in this once in a  generation opportunity once in a  lifetime opportunity to reverse  centuries of hurt to advance racial  justice um  you know we can pay for these things  there's not a deficit of resource there  is a deficit of empathy and  prioritization  so congresswoman if if  the taxing the rich part of this budget  reconciliation doesn't go far enough and  a lot of people are pointing out that  the house ways and means committee's  proposal doesn't go far enough for the  super rich will progressives like  yourself use your leverage in the same  way that mansion or cinema have in the  senate to block that  right now i'm focused on advancing these  progressive policies and the causes of  the my constituents and the american  people who are experiencing  unprecedented hurt so i'm staying at the  table i'm going to continue to fight for  this reconciliation to be as bold as  possible to meet the moment and to meet  the needs of the american people  and beyond that you know we shall see  but i don't until the ink is dry uh and  there's a vote immediately in front of  me what i'm focused on is just making  those uh making the case for why these  investments must be made it's critical  and again we have the majority and we  have a mandate and we need to act like  it  thank you so much we're out of time but  congresswoman ayanna presley appreciate  you coming on the show today  thank you

